//! Selection-adjusted change-point p-value calibration table.
//!
//! Generated by the `cargo-bench-history-calibration` crate. Do not edit by hand: run
//! `just bench-history-calibration-write` to regenerate, and see that crate's docs and
//! `cargo-bench-history`'s design appendix for the method.
//!
//! # Provenance
//!
//! * Procedure: Pettitt location over every interior split, `min_regime` rejection, then
//!   the two-sided Mann–Whitney p-value at the located split — the change-point detector's
//!   own procedure, evaluated on rank orderings (ties absent, so the tie term is zero).
//! * Rows: one per series length 10..=1000 (991 rows), no gaps.
//! * Small rows (n <= 11): exhaustive enumeration of all n! orderings — exact, no margin.
//! * Larger rows: 2000000 Monte Carlo orderings via the workspace splitmix64
//!   generator, seeded per row by FNV-1a over a fixed label.
//! * Conservativeness: a one-sided Dvoretzky–Kiefer–Wolfowitz band added to each sampled
//!   CDF, Bonferroni-split across the Monte Carlo rows at family level 0.01, so no row
//!   under-corrects (over the generation randomness). Where the band cannot certify a level,
//!   the ladder stops and deeper outcomes report its floor.
//! * Grid: 98 adjusted levels, geometric ratio 1.1, anchored exactly on
//!   0.05, spanning down to 0.0001, with an explicit 1.0 top rung.
//! * Rounding: each value is the shortest decimal that round-trips to the same f64, with a
//!   trailing `.0` on integers so every element parses as f64.

